This is a greedy assignment with a local-search style improvement, kept simple to stay within the time limit.

**Approach.** Process the vehicles by time. Repeatedly pick the vehicle that frees up earliest (a priority queue keyed on its free time). For that vehicle, scan all unassigned rides and choose the best feasible one, where feasible means the ride can still finish by its latest finish.

For each candidate ride:
- `arrive = t + dist(pos, start)`
- `st = max(arrive, s)`
- `end = st + d`, which must satisfy `end <= f`
- `score = d + (st == s ? B : 0)`

The ride is chosen by maximizing `score / (end - t)`, the points per time used, which accounts for both driving and waiting. If no ride is feasible for that vehicle, it is retired.

**Cost.** Each assignment scans up to N rides, and there are at most N assignments in total. That is 10^8 simple operations in the worst case, which is fine. Failed vehicles do one scan each and are then dropped. To keep scans cheap, the unassigned rides are held in a compact vector and removed by swap-and-pop.

**Tie-breaking.** Ties are broken by the earlier end time and then by index, so the output is deterministic. The ratio comparison uses cross-multiplication with `long long` to avoid floating point. Time values can reach 1e9 and scores about 2e4, so the products stay well within 64 bits.

**Ratio detail.** The denominator is `end - t`, which is at least 1 because `d >= 1`. Comparing `a.score * b.den > b.score * a.den` is therefore valid.

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
typedef long long ll;
int main(){
    int R,C,F,N,B;ll T;
    scanf("%d %d %d %d %d %lld",&R,&C,&F,&N,&B,&T);
    vector<array<int,6>> r(N);
    for(auto&x:r)for(int k=0;k<6;k++)scanf("%d",&x[k]);
    vector<int> un(N);
    for(int i=0;i<N;i++)un[i]=i;
    vector<vector<int>> res(F);
    vector<array<int,2>> pos(F,{0,0});
    vector<ll> tm(F,0);
    priority_queue<pair<ll,int>,vector<pair<ll,int>>,greater<>> pq;
    for(int i=0;i<F;i++)pq.push({0,i});
    while(!pq.empty()&&!un.empty()){
        auto [t,v]=pq.top();pq.pop();
        int px=pos[v][0],py=pos[v][1];
        int best=-1;ll bs=0,bd=1,be=0;
        for(int k=0;k<(int)un.size();k++){
            auto&x=r[un[k]];
            ll d=abs(x[2]-x[0])+abs(x[3]-x[1]);
            ll arrive=t+abs(x[0]-px)+abs(x[1]-py);
            ll st=max(arrive,(ll)x[4]);
            ll en=st+d;
            if(en>x[5])continue;
            ll sc=d+(st==x[4]?B:0);
            ll den=en-t;
            bool better=false;
            if(best<0)better=true;
            else{
                ll l=sc*bd,rr=bs*den;
                if(l>rr)better=true;
                else if(l==rr&&en<be)better=true;
            }
            if(better){best=k;bs=sc;bd=den;be=en;}
        }
        if(best<0)continue;
        int id=un[best];
        un[best]=un.back();un.pop_back();
        res[v].push_back(id);
        pos[v]={r[id][2],r[id][3]};
        pq.push({be,v});
    }
    for(int i=0;i<F;i++){
        printf("%d",(int)res[i].size());
        for(int x:res[i])printf(" %d",x);
        printf("\n");
    }
}
```
